# Code owners for ethereumclassic/core-geth.
#
# An owner listed here is requested for review automatically, and where the
# repository ruleset requires code owner review, one of them has to approve
# before a pull request can merge.
#
# The owner is a team rather than an account, for two reasons. GitHub does not
# let an author approve their own pull request, so a single-account owner has
# nobody who can satisfy the rule on that account's own changes. And membership
# then changes in one place, without a commit.
#
# The team must exist and hold write access to this repository before code
# owner review is required. GitHub ignores an owner it cannot resolve, and an
# unresolvable owner combined with a required code owner review blocks every
# pull request. The team is org-scoped rather than repository-scoped, so it can
# own the organization's other client repositories as they need it.
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the specific paths below override the
# catch-all rather than adding to it.

*                       @ethereumclassic/core-developers

# Consensus and chain configuration. A change here decides which chain a node
# follows, and a mistake is a split rather than a failing build.
/params/                @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/core/                  @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/consensus/             @ethereumclassic/core-developers

# Networking and the node's exposed surface.
/eth/                   @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/p2p/                   @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/rpc/                   @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/internal/ethapi/       @ethereumclassic/core-developers

# Consensus fixtures and the suites that read them.
/tests/                 @ethereumclassic/core-developers

# Anything that runs in CI with the organization's secrets, or that decides
# what a release contains.
/.github/               @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/build/                 @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/Dockerfile             @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/Dockerfile.alltools    @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/go.mod                 @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/go.sum                 @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/.gitmodules            @ethereumclassic/core-developers

# Licensing is a legal question before it is a technical one.
/COPYING                @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/COPYING.LESSER         @ethereumclassic/core-developers
/SECURITY.md            @ethereumclassic/core-developers

# Published documentation.
/docs/                  @ethereumclassic/core-developers
